  "pages": "p.2 (Figure 1 pinout), p.3-4 (pin descriptions; MULT(1:0) pins 38/39 named MUL0/MUL1 in the drawing), p.5 (operating ratings: VA 3.0-3.6 V, VDR 2.7 V to VA+0.3 V, VD/VP up to VA+0.3 V), p.10 (tODR 13.1 ns max, pipeline 6 clocks), p.14 (Figure 7 bypass timing), p.21 (straight binary, PD, PDADC, buffer flags), p.28-30 (buffer pins, DRDY, Tables 1-2)",
  "notModeled": [
    "analog input and reference ladder (the result is always the 0 V code 0x00)",
    "the 256/512/1024-byte capture buffer (BSIZE1/BSIZE0 not 00): WEN/REN/RCLK/ASW writing and reading, EF/FF flags, WENSYNC and RESET of the buffer pointers; the model is the buffer-bypassed mode (BSIZE1 = BSIZE0 = 0), where those inputs are ignored and EF/FF are held low (the model leaves EF, FF and WENSYNC undriven)",
    "PLL clock multiplier (MULT1/MULT0 x2/x4/x8): the model makes one conversion per CLK rising edge (PLL bypassed)",
    "pipeline latency of 6 clock cycles (the code is constant); DRDY edge selection by OEDGE/TEN (data change on DRDY rise when high, fall when low) and Test Mode (OEDGE/TEN at VA/2)",
    "PDADC (ADC-only power-down with the buffer still readable); PD high holds the outputs at the last byte (the model's powerdown only blocks conversions); 2-20 us wake-up",
    "vcc is VDR 2.7 V up to 3.6 V (the VA maximum); VD 'connect to +3.3 V' (max VA + 0.3 V); clock frequency limits"
  ],
